From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 13:15:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lavu/hwcontext_rkmpp: free the mapping on the non-linear
 reject path

rkmpp_map_frame() allocates its RKMPPDRMMapping before it inspects the
descriptor, then returns ENOSYS for a non-linear format modifier without
freeing it. Every AFBC or otherwise tiled frame offered to a CPU map leaks
the allocation; the caller has no way to reach it, because the descriptor
is only published through ff_hwframe_map_create() much further down.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 libavutil/hwcontext_rkmpp.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/libavutil/hwcontext_rkmpp.c b/libavutil/hwcontext_rkmpp.c
index a03f802..f82e00e 100644
--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_rkmpp.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_rkmpp.c
@@ -410,6 +410,7 @@ static int rkmpp_map_frame(AVHWFramesContext *hwfc,
 
     if (desc->drm_desc.objects[0].format_modifier != DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR) {
         av_log(hwfc, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Transfer non-linear DRM_PRIME frame is not supported!\n");
+        av_free(map);
         return AVERROR(ENOSYS);
     }
 
